    "add-a-page": "---\ntitle: Add a page\nsummary: Add a new page to your site, choose where it sits, and put it in your menu.\narea: pages\norder: 1\nrelated:\npopular: true\n---\nEvery page starts with a heading block, ready for you to add more.\n\n1. Open **Pages** in the sidebar.\n2. Press **New page** at the top right.\n3. Type the **Page title**, for example “Prices”. This becomes the page’s address too (/prices).\n4. If it belongs under another page, choose it in **Put it under**. Otherwise leave it as **Nothing (a main page)**.\n5. Press **Create and open**. The new page opens in the editor.\n6. Add blocks and words, then press **Publish** when you’re ready. Until then, visitors can’t see it.\n\n![The Pages screen with the New page form open](shot:pages-new)\n\n## Tips\n\n- New pages are added to your header menu automatically, unless you’ve set up your menus by hand.\n- To add a page under an existing one straight from the list, press the **+** next to that page.\n- Not ready to share it? Leave it unpublished: it shows as a draft in your Pages list.\n"
